      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "Jul",
      "dc:description": "Maintenance of surface mine equipment cannot be performed on a catch-as-catch can basis if production equipment is to perform at its optimum efficiency. Mine management must make use of every maintenance technique available if production ggoals that have been established for an operation are to be achieved. The most effective operational organization has but limited value if the production machinery cannot be maintained in running order; and the resultant downtime can quickly destroy the profit capability of that equipment.",
