      "prism:coverDate": "1973-01-01",
      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "Jun",
      "dc:description": "Rainfall to 45 to 48 in. per year, mostly occurring during the winter months, and a fine grain, readily erodible overburden are factors that have been effectively dealt with at Centralia mine in protecting the quality of a local stream important to migratory fish. A two-pond chemical flocculating system that is described protects stream integrity from surface run-off generated in the mine area.",
