      "prism:coverDate": "1971-01-01",
      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "June",
      "dc:description": "Designed to treat 5 million t per yr the Marcopper surface mine situated on the Island of Marinduque, approximately 110 air mi south of Manila, started production in Oct 1969. Ore reserves are calculated at about 150 million t graded between 0. 89 and 0. 28% Cu plus Au and Ag. Ore treatment by flotation is described and flowsheet and equipment specifications are included. Mineralized rock containing over 0. 2% Cu is heap- leached. Capital and operating costs are tabulated.",
