      "dc:title": "PAM motors. A special type used by IMC for phosphate- slurry pump drives",
      "dc:creator": "STOCKMAN RH",
      "prism:publicationName": "Engineering and Mining Journal",
      "prism:issn": "00958948",
      "prism:volume": "142",
      "prism:issueIdentifier": "1",
      "prism:pageRange": "77-79",
      "prism:coverDate": "1971-01-01",
      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "Jan",
      "dc:description": "Pole Amplitude Modulated (PAM) electric a- c motors, introduced bu Westinghouse Electric Corp are installed at the phosphate surface mine of International Minerals and Chemicals Corp, Bartow, Fla to drive centrifugal pumps, pipelining phosphate slurry from the mine to the processing plant. PAM motors can operate at nearly any speed combination in 2, 3, or even 4 speeds at favorable torque rates and higher electrical efficiency at lower revolutions per minute than those of previously used wound- rotor induction motors.",
