      "dc:description": "Pelletizing plant of the Minntac, taconite surface mine, located at Mountain Iron, Minn is being expanded to reach in 1972 annual production of 12 million tons of pellete (double of present). Very hard crude ore mined from the Lower-, Cherty and Slaty members of the Biwabik ion formation is crushed, comminuted, and concentrated by magnetic separation to meet the required in pellets 65% Fe and 5. 5% SiO//2 contents. Flow sheets of the concentrator are shown. Agglomeration lines indurate pellets at 2450 F, cool the product to 250 F, and reclaim 80% of process heat.",
