      "prism:coverDisplayDate": "Mar",
      "dc:description": "The nimba surface mine is located about 160 mi from the Atlantic coast of Liberia. Transportation of 3600 tph of ore over a distance of 1. 9 mi across mountainous terrain to the railroad, located about 2000 ft beneath uppermost levels of the ore bodies, is done by a steel cord, rubber belt conveyor 47 1/4 in. wide by 1 in. thick, reinforced by 68 each 3/8 in. diam steel ropes, divided in 4 flights following a spur down the ridge with total drop of 1772 ft with maximum belt slope set-up at 17**0. Details of control of belt slip, detection of thorn belt, running at 10 fps and belt repair techniques are given. Average mechanical efficiency in handling 55 million tons was in excess of 90%.",
